bilbo digest: answer a session's first prompt with what bilbo keeps on it.

[1mUsage:[22m
  [36mbilbo digest [--agy][39m

[1mOptions:[22m
      [1m--agy[22m  Read Antigravity's PreInvocation input and answer in its JSON

[2mA prompt hook runs it and hands it one JSON object on standard input, with[22m
[2msession_id and prompt. Every prompt after a session's first prints nothing.[22m

[1mOutput:[22m
  A list for each kind with an entry at its floor or over, each under its line:
  files: [2m<n>[22m may bear on this prompt, best first; bilbo read [2m<ref>[22m outlines one
  [2m<ref>[22m[1m [22m[2m<capture>[22m[1m [22m[2m<title>[22m      a file's row, by tabs
  [2m<ref>[22m[1m [22m[2m<day>[22m[1m [22m[2m<folder>[22m[1m [22m[2m<line>[22m  a row of a session or a note: its passage's
                               ref and day, its folder, and its outline's
                               line or the note's start. A fifth field,
                               note: [2m<text>[22m, is a note derive wrote of it
  [1msummary: [22m[2m<text>[22m              a row's last field: the summary derive wrote
                               of its entry, where there is one
  [1mdigest.log[22m                   in the state folder: one line a run

[1mExit:[22m
  [1m0[22m  always, so its exit code blocks no prompt; stderr says what went wrong

[1mExamples:[22m
  echo '{"session_id":"s1","prompt":"thin the carrot rows"}' | bilbo digest

[1mDocs:[22m [2mhttps://github.com/delucca/bilbo/wiki/Commands#digest[22m
